This path installs the CLI, scaffolds one example service, starts the generated resource graph,
and makes one visible edit.

{{ comp callout { type: "note", title: "Prerequisites" } }}
Install <strong><a href="https://docs.deno.com">Deno 2.x</a></strong>, the
<strong><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspire/">.NET Aspire CLI</a></strong>, and start
Docker before continuing. Aspire orchestrates the local resource graph; Postgres and the shared
cache run in Docker containers that Aspire starts for you.
{{ /comp }}

## 1. Install the CLI

```bash
deno install --global --allow-all --name netscript jsr:@netscript/cli{{ releaseSpecifier }}
```

## 2. Scaffold the workspace

```bash
netscript init my-app --db postgres --service --yes
```

The `--service` flag scaffolds the example oRPC service alongside the workspace. `--yes` accepts
the remaining defaults without prompts, including the `dashboard` app name and shared Redis cache
used below.

## 3. Start the resource graph

**Nothing runs until this step.**

```bash
cd my-app/aspire
aspire restore   # first run only
aspire start
```

Use the dashboard URL and one-time login token printed by `aspire start`. Wait until all four
resources report healthy — the Fresh app, example service, Postgres, and shared cache — then open
the Fresh app from its resource link. The page heading should read `my-app`.

{{ comp callout { type: "note", title: "Aspire comes before any database command" } }}
The AppHost must start Postgres before a migration, generation, or seed command can connect to it.
Continue with <a href="/data-persistence/how-to/database-migration/">Database migrations</a> when
you need the database workflow.
{{ /comp }}

## 4. Make your first change

Open `apps/dashboard/routes/(_components)/home-view.tsx`. Find the wrapped introductory sentence
that starts with `A generated NetScript workspace` and replace that sentence with
`This checkout dashboard is ours.` Save the file, then refresh the Fresh app URL from Aspire. The
new sentence should appear below the `my-app` heading while the app remains healthy.

[See how the web layer is structured](/web-layer/).

When you are finished, stop the AppHost from the `aspire/` directory:

```bash
aspire stop --apphost ./apphost.mts
```

Continue with [the Storefront tutorial](/tutorials/storefront/) or [the mental model](/concepts/).
